#VRML V2.0 utf8
# N20 rubber wheel, real vendor part (user-supplied listing): 34mm diameter,
# 3mm D-axis bore, 6.5mm tire width, 3.2g. Sized to that real spec (this
# supersedes an earlier 32mm/9mm placeholder that matched only this
# project's own board_geom.py WHEEL_DIA/WHEEL_THK clearance-notch
# constants, not a real part).
#
# FLAG FOR REVIEW: the board's wheel-clearance notch is still cut to the
# OLD 32mm/9mm figures (board_geom.py WHEEL_DIA/WHEEL_THK) -- a real 34mm
# wheel is 2mm larger in diameter than that notch allows and 2.5mm
# narrower than the notch width. The narrower tire fits fine; the larger
# diameter may rub the notch edge -- re-check clearance (or widen the
# notch) before relying on this fit mechanically. Not changed here since
# that's a real board-outline/mechanical change, not a cosmetic one.
#
# UNITS: this project's own WRL convention (see N20_Motor_Encoder.wrl) is
# 1 unit = 2.54mm. radius 17mm=6.6929, tire width 6.5mm=2.5591, hub
# (cosmetic only, not a real 3mm D-bore hole -- VRML primitives can't cut
# a hole) radius 4mm=1.5748, height 7mm=2.7559. Shaft-center offset
# 5mm=1.9685, Z=1.9685 (5mm real height, matches N20_Motor_Encoder.wrl's
# own shaft/body centerline height above the board).

Group { children [
    Transform {
      translation 1.9685 0.0000 1.9685
      rotation 0 0 1 -1.5708
      children Shape {
        appearance Appearance { material Material { diffuseColor 0.08 0.08 0.08 } }
        geometry Cylinder { radius 6.6929 height 2.5591 }
      }
    }
    Transform {
      translation 1.9685 0.0000 1.9685
      rotation 0 0 1 -1.5708
      children Shape {
        appearance Appearance { material Material { diffuseColor 0.55 0.55 0.55 } }
        geometry Cylinder { radius 1.5748 height 2.7559 }
      }
    }
] }
